course: dictionary
lesson: 12976
title: Exhilarating: a word for joy and speed
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: «The roller coaster was exhilarating.» Think about what happens on a roller coaster: fast drops, loud screams and a racing heart. So exhilarating means it makes you feel very happy, excited and full of energy.
explain: Exhilarating is an adjective, and it comes from the verb exhilarate. To exhilarate someone is to make them feel very happy and full of energy. An exhilarating ride is one that does this to you.
explain: The word can also mean thrilling in a fast, fresh or slightly scary way. «Swimming in the cold sea was exhilarating.» The sea is cold and the feeling is sharp and fresh, so the word fits. Ask yourself: would thrilling fit here? If it does, you have the right meaning.
fact: Exhilarating is an adjective, and it comes from the verb exhilarate.
fact: «Exhilarate» means to make someone feel very happy, excited and full of energy.
fact: «Exhilarating» can mean thrilling in a fast, fresh or slightly scary way, like a ride, a race or a cold wind.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, Toad finds his first ride in a motor-car exhilarating.
fact: Mole finds his first day on the river exhilarating too, full of joy and freedom.
exercise: «The cold wind on the hill was exhilarating.» What does exhilarating mean here? | *Thrilling and fresh, full of energy | Quiet and sleepy | Hot and heavy | Boring and grey
exercise: Which word is the verb form of exhilarating? | Exhale | Exhaust | *Exhilarate | Exhibit
exercise: Ella says, «Her first swim in the cold sea was exhilarating.» What feeling does this show? | *Joy and excitement | Fear with no fun at all | Anger | Tiredness
test: «The roller coaster was exhilarating, and I screamed with joy.» What does exhilarating show? | *Excitement and happiness | Sleepiness | Hunger | Boredom
test: Which sentence uses exhilarating correctly? | The soup was exhilarating and cold. | The library was exhilarating and quiet. | The sleepy cat was exhilarating. | *The last-minute goal was exhilarating for the whole crowd.
exam: «Mole's first day on the river was exhilarating.» What does exhilarating mean in this sentence? | Cold and wet | Dull and slow | *Full of joy, excitement and energy | Sad and lonely
